    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48556" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θετέος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to
				be countedas</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Epin.</u>
				984a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1277b38
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θετέον</span>, <i>one must
			establish</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἆθλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					832e
				</span></i>
			; <i>one must assume</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				4.2.15
			</span></i>; <i>one must reckon, count</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς βαναύσους πολίτας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1277b35
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Satyr.
				<u>Vit.Eur.Fr.</u>
				39xv6
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ἁμαρτίᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.171
				</span></i>
			.</div>
